# qcom-atel-ready is a system_ext helper (see atel-ready/Android.bp) that sends
# the QCRIL_EVT_HOOK_SET_ATEL_UI_STATUS OEM hook to qcril. Without it qcril holds
# every incoming SMS in its power optimisation buffer and drops it
# unacknowledged; see the comment in atel-ready/qcom-atel-ready.cpp.
#
# The domain is declared in sepolicy/public/qcom_atel_ready.te because this
# vendor policy has to reference it. The helper runs against the system
# servicemanager, where qcrild publishes
# vendor.qti.hardware.radio.qcrilhook.IQtiOemHook/oemhook{0,1}. The
# service_manager entry is labeled vendor_hal_telephony_service2, but the
# binder call itself lands in the qcrild process, which runs as rild; without
# the rild rule every oemHookRawRequest fails with PERMISSION_DENIED and qcril
# never learns that the telephony UI is ready.
allow qcom_atel_ready vendor_hal_telephony_service2:service_manager find;

binder_call(qcom_atel_ready, vendor_hal_telephony_service2)
binder_call(qcom_atel_ready, rild)
